The matrix above is supported by a delivery order tailored to AD-488. Functional and integration tests begin in Dev and QA to validate gating, upload acceptance, crop parameter handling, MIME and magic-number checks, and gateway routing. Security and compliance controls are then expanded in QA and Pre-Prod to validate malware handling, unauthorized rejection, and audit events. Performance and business E2E execution are sequenced after service integration stabilizes because valid timing evidence requires representative end-to-end orchestration rather than stubbed dependencies.

Playwright will be used as the primary browser automation framework for UI, SPA refresh, and multi-session synchronization validation. PyTest will orchestrate API, gateway, storage, and log-based assertions. JMeter will generate controlled performance and concurrency traffic for 4G-throttled SLA evidence. OWASP ZAP will support negative security validation and upload-surface inspection. tcconfig will enforce network-shaping conditions so SLA evidence reflects the stated 4G proxy boundary. Together, these tools provide layered architectural coverage aligned to the required test levels rather than overlapping generic automation.

